## CaDiCaL is vendored in src/cadical/ and built from source.
##
## Every -D flag below replaces something CaDiCaL's own ./configure would
## have detected or generated. We deliberately do not ship a configure
## script, so each one is set unconditionally:
##
##   NBUILD     CaDiCaL's makefile generates build.hpp via a shell script
##              that needs git and a build subdirectory. version.cpp
##              supports NBUILD to skip it and use a compiled-in version.
##   NDEBUG     disable assertions (configure sets this unless --check).
##   QUIET      drop the verbose solver logging machinery.
##   NTRACING   drop proof-tracing support we do not expose.
##   NCLOSEFROM use the portable fd-closing loop in file.cpp. Without this
##              the build fails on macOS: closefrom(3) is not declared.
##   NUNLOCKED  do not use getc_unlocked/putc_unlocked.
##   ZUSAT_NO_PIPES
##              compile out the compressed-file paths in file.cpp, which
##              fork and exec gzip/xz and _exit() in the child. zusat never
##              opens a file through CaDiCaL, and R CMD check rejects _exit.

## Every .cpp lives in cadical/, and R CMD INSTALL only globs src/*.c* --
## it never sees them, so it would link the .so with the C compiler and
## leave every C++ standard-library symbol undefined. That happens to work
## wherever R has already loaded libstdc++, and fails at dlopen on the
## libc++ toolchains: "undefined symbol: _ZNSt3__19to_stringEj". Declaring
## CXX_STD is what tells R this is a C++ package, so it links with CXX.
## The standard is pinned to 14 rather than R's default of 17 for a second
## reason. libstdc++ 12 implements std::stable_sort -- which CaDiCaL calls in
## about ten places -- over std::get_temporary_buffer, and C++17 deprecates
## that. clang then reports a deprecation inside libstdc++'s own header, and
## R CMD check escalates it to "Found the following significant warnings",
## failing the build. Before C++17 the deprecation does not exist, so the
## warning does not arise. Suppressing it instead is not an option: a
## -Wno-* flag trips "checking compilation flags used", which rejects flags
## that suppress warnings. CaDiCaL itself only requires C++11, and its own
## configure builds with -std=c++11, so 14 asks for nothing it lacks.
CXX_STD = CXX14

PKG_CPPFLAGS = -I. -Icadical -DNBUILD -DNDEBUG -DQUIET -DNTRACING \
               -DNCLOSEFROM -DNUNLOCKED -DZUSAT_NO_PIPES

## CADICAL_OBJECTS is an explicit list generated by tools/vendor-cadical.sh.
## It is not built with $(wildcard), which R CMD check flags as a GNU make
## extension.
include cadical/objects.mk

OBJECTS = zusat.o init.o $(CADICAL_OBJECTS)
